From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:29:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): filter the sidebar to sessions updated recently

The sidebar lists every session and every project folder, so a long-lived
sidebar buries what changed lately. The Updated grouping can surface it,
but it is release-flagged and drops the project folders.

Add a device-local "Updated" filter to the sessions filter menu,
alongside the My/Shared/All/Archived scope and independent of the
grouping flag: Any time / Last 24 hours / Last 3 days / Last 7 days /
Last 30 days. These are rolling windows, not calendar days, so the
shortest one doesn't empty out just after midnight. The choices live in
one ordered table, so another window is a one-line addition.

While it is on, project folders with nothing matching are hidden, the
filter icon is highlighted, and the open session stays listed. Pins are
unaffected, as with the scope filter.

The active window also shows as a chip beside the filter button (24h,
3d, 7d or 30d), so a short list reads as filtered at a glance. The chip
is a button that clears the filter; activated from the keyboard, it
hands focus back to the filter button.

Carried on custom until it lands upstream; cut from upstream/main as
feat/sidebar-attention-filters. Drop this copy once merged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
